[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known as one parser bug. Read by tenant, channel and body, its reports are three
problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 does not close the other two problems.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates
  come out with day and month swapped, on every channel and both booking forms.
- **`hint`**: `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first
  tenants type what the hint says, and the form reads it day first. Only reports sent through the
  form, only at tenants on `booking-v3`. The parser fix leaves this as it is; the hint has to
  change.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day, not by a month swap. Reporters describe Monday for
  Tuesday, a client in Toronto getting a different day than one in Lisbon, an invite that arrives
  before the booking. That points at time zones, not at date order. The desk had footnoted these
  under `parser`.

## For the desk

- Intake's `intakeTag` is a guess from the reporter's browser. File by tenant and channel
  (`#lib/kb/causes.ts`), and read the body when the date moved by one day.
- Same subject does not mean same problem: all three share subjects like "Wrong day on the
  invite".

